# Quality tooling (agent)

Canon: `docs/products/ERA-Acceptance-Standard.md` § Tooling.

## Before «done» / PR

1. `npm run check:acceptance` (strict: `npm run check:acceptance:strict`)
2. On MDM / hub / workforce / reference contracts: `npm run audit:integration:strict`
3. Design tokens (if UI): `npm run lint:design-tokens` + `npm run lint:token-layers`
4. Bundle: `npm run run:quality-gates`
5. Matrix: no Scaffold ✅ without negative path; no false `all ✅`; no edition `ga` without Pilot-ready
6. Pick-list UI: no new `shortText`/`code` for catalog-shaped fields — use `CatalogField` + `CatalogFieldKind` (`era-managed-list-controls.mdc`)

## Shell bans (also in hooks)

- `git push --force`, `git reset --hard`, `git clean -f` without explicit user request
- `git stash` without explicit user request (legal-entities / unrelated WIP)
- Emergency reset of a core to `origin/dev` for CI green — forbidden (`era-no-emergency-reset`)
- DROP/TRUNCATE DB; wipe volumes on `*prod*` compose

## Artifacts

| What | Where |
|------|-------|
| Hooks | `.cursor/hooks.json` |
| Skills | `.cursor/skills/acceptance-closeout`, `quality-gates` |
| Consistency | `scripts/check-acceptance-consistency.mjs` |
| Config | `kit-config.yaml` |

Do not add phone-home telemetry to product runtime. Scanners stay offline/local/CI.
